{"lesson": {"title": "Why bubble sort is O(n²)", "goal": "See that bubble sort compares every pair, so n numbers need n(n-1)/2 looks, which grows like n squared.", "labs": ["array"]}}
{"step": 1, "say": "Bubble sort puts numbers in order with one tiny move, repeated. Look at two neighbors. If the left one is bigger, they trade places.", "scene": {"arr": {"lab": "array", "values": [5, 1, 4, 2, 3], "counters": ["comparisons"]}}, "do": [{"cue": "two neighbors", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "trade places", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}]}
{"step": 2, "say": "Here is the whole algorithm. The outer loop sets a wall, i, at the far end. The inner loop slides j along the pairs. If the left value is bigger, swap.", "scene": {"code": {"kind": "code", "language": "python", "source": "for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n    for j in range(i):\n        if a[j] > a[j + 1]:\n            a[j], a[j + 1] = a[j + 1], a[j]"}}, "do": [{"cue": "outer loop", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[1]"]}, {"cue": "outer loop", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "i", "to": 4}, {"cue": "inner loop", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[2]"]}, {"cue": "inner loop", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 1}, {"cue": "bigger", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[3]"]}, {"cue": "swap", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[4]"]}]}
{"step": 3, "say": "The pointer j is on the five. Five against four: bigger, so swap. Five against two, swap again. Five against three, and the last swap. The five has bubbled to the end, done for good.", "do": [{"cue": "against four", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[3]"]}, {"cue": "against four", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "so swap", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[4]"]}, {"cue": "so swap", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"cue": "against two", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 2}, {"cue": "against two", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[3]"]}, {"cue": "against two", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "swap again", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[4]"]}, {"cue": "swap again", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"cue": "against three", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 3}, {"cue": "against three", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[3]"]}, {"cue": "against three", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "last swap", "op": "focus", "on": ["code[4]"]}, {"cue": "last swap", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"]}, {"cue": "done for good", "op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[4]"]}, {"cue": "done for good", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "i", "to": 3}, {"cue": "done for good", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 0}]}
{"step": 4, "say": "Pass two runs the same way, one cell shorter. One against four, no swap. Four against two, so swap. Four against three, swap again. Now four is home.", "do": [{"cue": "One against four", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "Four against two", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 1}, {"cue": "Four against two", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "so swap", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"cue": "Four against three", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 2}, {"cue": "Four against three", "op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"cue": "swap again", "op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"cue": "is home", "op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[3]"]}, {"cue": "is home", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "i", "to": 2}, {"cue": "is home", "op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 0}]}
{"step": 5, "say": "Passes three and four look at what is left, two pairs and then one. Nothing moves. The looks still happen, and each one is counted.", "do": [{"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 1}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "i", "to": 1}, {"op": "pointer", "on": ["arr"], "name": "j", "to": 0}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[0-4]"]}, {"op": "clear", "on": ["arr"], "what": "pointers"}]}
{"step": 6, "say": "Add up the looks. Four, then three, then two, then one. Ten comparisons for five numbers.", "scene": {"code": null, "eq": {"kind": "math", "latex": "4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 10"}}, "do": [{"cue": "Ten comparisons", "op": "pulse", "on": ["eq"]}]}
{"step": 7, "say": "For n numbers, the looks add up to n times n minus one, over two. Ten numbers need forty-five. Twenty need one hundred ninety, about four times as many.", "do": [{"cue": "For n numbers", "op": "morph", "on": ["eq"], "into": {"kind": "math", "latex": "(n-1) + (n-2) + \\cdots + 1 = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}"}}]}
{"step": 8, "say": "Now eight numbers in the worst order, backwards. Before I run it, predict: how many comparisons will bubble sort make?", "scene": {"eq": null, "arr": {"lab": "array", "values": [8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1], "counters": ["comparisons"]}}, "challenge": {"kind": "predict", "type": "number", "prompt": "How many comparisons for these eight numbers?", "answer": 28}}
{"step": 9, "say": "Watch the counter climb. Every pair gets compared, and in this order every pair also swaps. The biggest value bubbles up first, then the next, and the next, until everything is home. Twenty-eight looks.", "do": [{"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[5]", "arr[6]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[5]", "arr[6]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[6]", "arr[7]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[6]", "arr[7]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[7]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[5]", "arr[6]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[5]", "arr[6]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[6]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[4]", "arr[5]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[5]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[3]", "arr[4]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[4]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[2]", "arr[3]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[3]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[1]", "arr[2]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[2]"]}, {"op": "compare", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"], "count": "comparisons"}, {"op": "swap", "on": ["arr[0]", "arr[1]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[1]"]}, {"op": "sorted", "on": ["arr[0]"]}]}
{"step": 10, "say": "Eight numbers took twenty-eight looks, exactly eight times seven over two. That grows like n squared, so bubble sort is O of n squared. Double the numbers and the work roughly quadruples.", "scene": {"eq": {"kind": "math", "latex": "\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; O(n^2)"}}, "do": [{"cue": "O of n squared", "op": "pulse", "on": ["eq"]}]}
